        "details": "Jahan, the answer is THREE (3). And here\u2019s why.\u00a0\r\n\r\nThree years is enough time to truly test and explore the absolute possibilities of a niche.\u00a0\r\n\r\nRemember that you can expand and contract a niche. Niches are ever-growing and ever-changing things. They are NOT as static as you think they are.\u00a0\r\n\r\nAnd when you pick the right niche, aka the one that has:\r\n\r\na) Enough volume\r\n\r\nb) They\u2019re contactable\r\n\r\nc) They\u2019re specific\u00a0\r\n\r\nYou\u2019re \r\n\r\n**golden**.\r\n\r\nSure, there might be competition. But there\u2019s enough volume to beat it.\u00a0\r\n\r\nSure, they might be on other sales calls. But they\u2019re contactable enough to beat it.\u00a0\r\n\r\nSure, others might be targeting them too. But they\u2019re specific enough that you can go and find more of them.\u00a0\r\n\r\nOn the flipside, the worst niche is the one you\u2026\r\n\r\n**PICKED before time has elapsed\u2026**\r\n\r\nOr you rushed in just to \r\n\r\n**\u201cdo something.\u201d**\r\n\r\nSeriously, make a strong, grounded decision in WHO your niche is.\u00a0\r\n\r\nWe\u2019ve got over 4,000 specific, strong niches for you to choose from. So if you want to grow your business in FULL confidence, click here and connect with us. https://app.iclosed.io/e/imperium/discovery-call-o\r\n\r\nAlternatively, check this out.\r\n\r\nMy general preference is B2B markets because they\u2019re immediately specific.\u00a0\r\n\r\nA \r\n\r\n**fantastic** B2B market, immediately, is a chiropractor. Why?\r\n\r\nBecause you either are one, or you\u2019re not. You can\u2019t \r\n\r\n**really** fake it.\u00a0\r\n\r\nIt\u2019s as if you wear a label over your head, and I can immediately spot you, and start a conversation with you. Make sense?\r\n\r\nWhen you\u2019re NOT in a B2B market, things \r\n\r\n**can** get tough(er) because your market is broad. It\u2019s the everyday person.\u00a0\r\n\r\nSay you\u2019re a fitness coach\u2026 start asking yourself WHO is your client?\r\n\r\nTechnically, it\u2019s everybody. Anybody and everybody can work with a coach, regardless of their shape, size or goals.\u00a0\r\n\r\nBut what I tend to find is people hyperfixating on \r\n\r\n**demographics** at this level. \u201cOh, they\u2019re 37, drive a BMW, and they\u2019re ma",
