        "summary": "EMERGENCY - Please Respond",
        "subject": "EMERGENCY - Please Respond",
        "details": "Dear Jonathan\r\n\r\nGood morning. I am Jahan Taila's father, we briefly spoke yesterday and I\r\nam writing to you in accordance with your request.\r\n\r\nYesterday, about 6 p.m. I visited my son's assigned apartment located\r\nat 1501 Bellamy Pl, Louisville, KY 40208, because of the horrendous and\r\nabsolutely  dangerous living conditions directly caused by one of the\r\nroommates open use of drugs.\r\n\r\nUpon entering Jahan's apartment, I was overcome by a strong stench of\r\nMarijuana, there was an unknown white male about 21 years of age sleeping\r\non the sofa in the living room who woke up after hearing me ask about who\r\nthis person was to Jahan and Nathan Anil who is Jahan's friend and\r\nroommate. This unknown white male was crystal clearly under the influence\r\nof an illegal substance.\r\n\r\nOn the chair adjacent to the sofa, I observed a huge pile of clothes with\r\nsome clothes laying on the floor of the living room. Upon inquiry, I found\r\nout that none of the items belonged to Jahan or Nathan Anil, both of whom\r\nare new students at University of Louisville. The entire apartment smells\r\nof Marijuana, end of discussion.\r\n\r\nI briefly spoke to the roommate directly responsible for creating this\r\nnon-liviable condition. By the very looks, his appearance in itself made it\r\nclear to me that he is a heavy drug user, there is NO DOUBT in my mind.\r\n\r\nMy son's and Nathan Anil's academic performance and career is at stake.\r\nFurthermore, the inaction on your part and that of Derby Row and its\r\nofficers and employees is completely and absolutely unacceptable to me.\r\n\r\nBoth, Jahan Taila, my son and Nathan Anil are in fear of their well-being\r\nand academic performance. Jahan, has been sleeping at his friend's house\r\nand Nathan Anil sleep's at his parents residence. This is NOT acceptable.\r\n\r\nEvery residence, place of living is incumbered by the rule of habitability\r\nunder the law. It is evident that Derby Row had prior knowledge of the\r\nbehavior and conduct of this questionable roommate, and yet Derby Row has\r\nNOT taken any legal action against him. WHY?\r\n\r\nDerby Row is in breach of the terms and conditions of the lease and the\r\napplicable covenants governing Landlord-Tenant relationship.\r\n\r\nI have had extensive conversations with Jahan's mother and Mr. Jans, Nathan\r\nAnil's father both of whom visited the apartment last weekend and\r\nimmediately raised serious concerns about the same in their emails to Derby\r\nRow and to you in particular.\r\n\r\nThe academic year began just yesterday (Monday, August 18th) and they\r\nshould NOT be at the receiving end of somebody else's nefarious conduct. We\r\ncannot wait till Derby Row exercises its legal right to evict this roommate\r\nwhose conduct shocks a human conscience.\r\n\r\nHence, I want my son and Nathan Anil to be assigned a two (2) bedroom\r\napartment immediately at a reasonable rate. This is of paramount importance\r\nbecause time is of essence. We as concern parents hope Derby Row shall make\r\nthis their first priority today!\r\n\r\nShould you have an",
