      {
        "id": "email-230-0",
        "type": "email",
        "date": "2025-11-05",
        "summary": "Get $5,500 Waived Onboarding Fee For Motion Teams",
        "subject": "Get $5,500 Waived Onboarding Fee For Motion Teams",
        "details": "Hi there,\r\n\r\n\u00a0\r\n\r\nOur customers consistently say Motion provides the \"single best vendor onboarding we've ever had.\"\r\n\r\n\u00a0\r\n\r\nWe invest a ton of resources into customer onboarding because we know from having experienced it ourselves: a project work management tool is only as good as the process it runs on.\r\n\r\n\u00a0\r\n\r\nMotion AI Project Manager is the most advance planning tool because it relies on an algorithmic optimization engine that scans your calendar and your team's calendars thousands of times each day to constantly deliver the ideal schedule for maximizing the chances you hit all your competing deadlines.\r\n\r\n\u00a0\r\n\r\nNo one else does this. Come see it for yourself and book a demo today ( https://cal.com/forms/b47915b0-44dd-495b-81b0-4e0c7aa5dbd7 ). We will waive your onboarding fees ($5.5K) if you use the link. Sometimes our sales team get annoyed with me and my promises. \ud83d\ude44\r\n\r\n\u00a0\r\n\r\nI'll finish off with one of my favorite customer quotes on onboarding:\r\n\r\n\u00a0\r\n\r\n\"Y'all are the best at implementation support we've had. Often times with other vendors, we sign the paperwork with some sales guy, and they are like \"cya!\" Motion's onboarding is very structured - training for execs, managers, and employee ICs are done in separate sessions.\"\r\n- CEO, MP Cloud\u00a0\r\n\r\n\u00a0\r\n\r\nBest,\r\n\r\nGary\r\n\r\n\u200aUnsubscribe ( https://track.customer.io/unsubscribe/dgSbpwcAANqUkALZlJACAZpUG4jf6XjFTKnHBCFIXw== )",
        "direction": "inbound",
        "createdAt": "2026-03-16T12:18:59"
      },
      {
        "id": "email-230-1",
        "type": "email",
        "date": "2025-11-02",
        "summary": "Love At First 18+ Completed Project Tasks",
        "subject": "Love At First 18+ Completed Project Tasks",
        "details": "Hi there,\r\n\r\n\u00a0\r\n\r\nGary again.\u00a0The first time I used Motion and saw the reshuffling of tasks I thought wow this is pretty neat.\r\n\r\n\u00a0\r\n\r\nBut I truly got excited when the end of the day came and I saw over 18+ completed tasks - making me swell up in excitement.\r\n\r\nThat's why I'm here today. To let people know (shouting from the rooftops) how crazy good this tool is.\r\n\r\nNot just for individuals. But also for teams of all sizes. We've even seen 140+ person teams completely move\u00a0their operating procedures into Motion. And\u00a0boy does it make project and work management easier.\r\n\r\nI'll pause there because you might be more interested in hearing what some of our customers are saying:\r\n\r\n*\r\n\"We evaluated the top-rated platforms\u2014Asana, Trello, ClickUp, Monday\u2014and none of them could compete with Motion\u2019s AI-driven task auto-scheduling, project workflow automations, incredibly fast interface, and comprehensive features. The way it automates resource-planning and schedules tasks based on your team\u2019s priorities, workload, and availability is next-level. Plus, they release new features at an incredibly rapid pace, so it keeps getting better. It\u2019s the perfect fit for companies that need a smart, efficient way to manage projects and tasks.\" - CEO at Ally Communications\r\n* \u201cWe had Asana for project management, but our team didn\u2019t use it regularly. Now, we have Motion and love it. It does everything Asana does and includes tools that make us more efficient. Plus, everyone actually uses it, because it integrates with our calendars.\u201d - Owner at Efficient App\r\n\u00a0\r\n\r\nIn my next email I'll share with you our best offer for teams since you've made it this far. Hope you check off some tasks today.\u00a0\r\n\r\n\u00a0\r\n\r\nCiao,\r\n\r\nGary\r\n\r\nIf you want to book a demo with our team click here ( https://cal.com/forms/b47915b0-44dd-495b-81b0-4e0c7aa5dbd7 )\r\n\r\n\u200aUnsubscribe ( https://track.customer.io/unsubscribe/dgSbpwcAANqUkALZlJACAZpEqGlUT9I_wTY4iVpGpg== )",
        "direction": "inbound",
        "createdAt": "2026-03-16T12:18:59"
      },
      {
        "id": "email-230-2",
        "type": "email",
        "date": "2025-10-31",
        "summary": "Motion x You",
        "subject": "Motion x You",
        "details": "Hi there,\r\n\r\n\u00a0\r\n\r\nGary again.\u00a0In the last 30d I've talked to 170+ teams in the workplace complaining about delaying their project deadlines, wasting time on project coordination, and even scraping work management tools that no one uses correctly (or often enough).\r\n\r\n\u00a0\r\n\r\nHere is what I've learned on how to stop the bleeding.\r\n\r\n\u00a0\r\n\r\nProject management or work management software is only as good as the process it runs on.\r\n\r\n\u00a0\r\n\r\nIf the team isn't using the software diligently - it doesn't matter what amazing features you were sold on.\r\n\r\n\u00a0\r\n\r\nThis is what our customers complain about\u00a0most often when they speak to us. Does anything sound relatable?\r\n\r\n*\r\nMassive backlog in emails means lots of time spent going back-and-forth on scheduling and admin tasks\r\n* Lots of manual processes makes the team rely on increasing headcount rather than streamlining and automating workflows\r\n*\r\nLast-minute changes from clients require lots of scrambling and ad-hoc comms to execute\r\n* Frequently miss client / customer project deadline by multiple weeks\r\n* Lack of ability to accurately forecast when a project will be finished\r\n*\r\nDifficulty managing multiple projects in different stages at once while trying to evaluate how many (and which) people are over or under capacity\r\n* Lack of visibility in knowing what people are working on. Lots of manual follow-ups needed\r\n*\r\nLack of transparency makes it easy for slackers to get by. And, frustration over contractors or employees delivering minimal work while being overcompensated\r\n\u00a0\r\n\r\nIf it does sound familiar know that you're not alone. When you manage projects by \"DUE\" date instead of \"DO\" date it's easy for projects to break down as complexity increases.\r\n\r\n\u00a0\r\n\r\nIn my next message, I'll show you exactly how other companies have fixed this problem on Motion.\r\n\r\n\u00a0\r\n\r\nBest,\r\n\r\nGary\r\n\r\nIf you want to book a demo with our team click here ( https://cal.com/forms/b47915b0-44dd-495b-81b0-4e0c7aa5dbd7 )\r\n\r\n\u200aUnsubscribe ( https://track.customer.io/unsubscribe/dgSbpwcAANqUkALZlJACAZo6W6dvJVgiBte5MneE6A== )",
        "direction": "inbound",
        "createdAt": "2026-03-16T12:18:59"
      },
      {
        "id": "email-230-3",
        "type": "email",
        "date": "2025-10-29",
        "summary": "Motion <> You - Project Management",
        "subject": "Motion <> You - Project Management",
        "details": "Hi there,\r\n\r\n\u00a0\r\n\r\nGary here from Motion -- contacting you with some big news!\r\n\r\n\u00a0\r\n\r\nWe've released an advanced version of Motion for teams size >15. Thousands of customers are getting onboarded this week and I wanted to make sure you got a chance to see what it's capable of.\r\n\r\n\u00a0\r\n\r\nIn short, this is why Motion for Team project and task management is unique:\r\n\r\n\u00a0\r\n\r\n*\r\nDO date \u2260 DUE date: give teammates real, actionable plans of what they need to do each day and week automatically rather than a far-out deadline they need to hit.\r\n*\r\nFull visibility & accountability for your entire team, automatically: see in real-time what teammates are working on and will prioritize. Full transparency eliminates the need to micromanage via status updates, emails, and messages.\r\n*\r\nPredict the future: we're the only project manager in the market that can predict if a project will meet the deadline 6 weeks or even 6 months in advance. Giving project managers unprecedented visibility and accountability into team capacity.\r\n*\r\nReal work, not Busy work: studies show that employees spend up to 50% of their time on \"work about work,\" such as reprioritizing tasks, attending meetings, and sending updates. Motion\u2019s project-level AI-based optimization engine creates an ideal plan for each team member based on project priorities, deadlines, and dependencies.\r\n*\r\nEveryone will love following SOPs: with customizable pre-built templates and AI-assisted workflow creation, you can transfer your SOPs and processes into Motion templates within minutes, reducing time spent on repetitive tasks and ensuring your team can start using Motion on day 1, not after a month of software training.\r\n\u00a0\r\n\r\nOver the next week, I'll be sharing more insight into how Motion's project management philosophy and software is a paradigm shift. Simply put, think of managing projects by \"DO\" date instead of \"DUE\" date.\r\n\r\n\u00a0\r\n\r\nLooking forward to sharing more!\r\n\r\n\u00a0\r\n\r\nBest,\r\n\r\nGary\r\n\r\nIf you want to book a demo with our team click here ( https://cal.com/forms/b47915b0-44dd-495b-81b0-4e0c7aa5dbd7 )\r\n\r\n\u200aUnsubscribe ( https://track.customer.io/unsubscribe/dgSbpwcAANqUkALZlJACAZowDu2e4P1HnH_-uozgtg== )",
        "direction": "inbound",
        "createdAt": "2026-03-16T12:18:59"
      }
