        "subject": "Why Your Website Isn't Generating Leads \u2013 And How to Fix It",
        "details": "Diese E-Mail im Browser ansehen (https://mailchi.mp/onepage/websites-die-vertrauen-schaffen-en-4763274?e=1d90d3ccee)\r\n\r\nHello\r\nJahan,\r\nYou have a website. It looks good. But the leads just aren\u2019t coming in.\r\n\r\nYou're not alone. Most websites have the same problem \u2013 and most of the time, it's not about the design or the copy. It's the structure.\r\n\r\nMost websites inform \u2013 but they don't lead the visitor to take action. A page that converts does something different. It guides the visitor through a thought process: Am I in the right place? Can they help me? Can I trust them? What do I do next?\r\n\r\nIf your page doesn't answer these questions \u2013 in the right order \u2013 the visitor leaves without reaching out.\r\n\r\nTwo rules make the difference:\r\n\r\n\ud83d\udccc Rule #1: One page, one goal.\r\n\r\nEvery element serves a single action \u2013 book a call, fill out a form, get in touch. The moment you add a second goal, you create uncertainty. And uncertainty kills conversions.\r\n\r\n\ud83d\udccc Rule #2: Order matters.\r\n\r\nTrust doesn't happen randomly. It\u2019s built section by section. Each part of your page has a job \u2013 and together, they build momentum. Break that flow, and you lose the lead.\r\n\r\nHere's what to do instead\ud83d\udc47\r\n\r\n\r\n** How to build a page that converts \u2013 section by section\r\n------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\n1\ufe0f\u20e3 Hero \u2013 \"Am I in the right place?\"\r\n\r\nYou have three seconds. That's it.\r\n\r\nYour headline shouldn't describe what you do \u2013 it should describe the problem you solve and the result the visitor can expect. One clear CTA. And a real photo of yourself or your team \u2013 not a stock image. Real faces build trust faster than any copy.\r\n\r\n2\ufe0f\u20e3 Social Proof \u2013 Credibility before doubt kicks in\r\n\r\nBefore visitors even decide whether to trust you, they're already scanning for proof. Logos, numbers, awards \u2013 placed early \u2013 answer that question before it even forms. Others have been here. They made a good decision.\r\n\r\n3\ufe0f\u20e3 Problem \u2013 \"They get me\"\r\n\r\nThis section isn't about you. It's about y",
        "direction": "inbound",
        "createdAt": "2026-03-16T12:18:59"
