        "details": "Diese E-Mail im Browser ansehen (https://mailchi.mp/onepage/forms-funnels-feature-en-4763254?e=1d90d3ccee)\r\n\r\nHello\r\nJahan,\r\nYou invest time, budget, and energy in reach. Campaigns are optimized, content is created, traffic is driven to your website \u2013 and visitors arrive.\r\n\r\nAnd yet, there\u2019s often a feeling that things could perform better.\r\n\r\nMore qualified inquiries. More conversions. More predictability.\r\n\r\nThis is exactly where Forms & Funnels comes in. Not as an additional tool next to your website, but as an integrated system that turns a simple form into a guided, automated process.\r\n\r\nMore than 8,400,000 leads have already been collected with this system. \ud83e\udd2f\r\n\r\nIn this newsletter, we show you how Forms & Funnels can not only increase your conversion rate but also significantly improve lead quality \u2013 with the same traffic.\r\n\r\nReady for a new perspective? \ud83d\udca1\r\n\r\n\r\n** Forms & Funnels: One System Instead of Five Tools\r\n------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\nMany companies today work with a patchwork of tools: an external form tool, a separate CRM, a booking system, additional tracking tools, automations via third-party providers \u2013 and in the end, all somehow has to be connected.\r\n\r\nThat means:\r\n\r\nWebsite + Form + CRM + Automation\r\n\r\nEvery interface becomes a potential source of errors. Every change costs time. Every integration increases complexity.\r\n\r\nForms & Funnels takes a different approach:\r\n\r\nWebsite + Form + Funnel + CRM + Tracking \u2192 in one integrated system\r\n\r\nNo design breaks due to embedded forms. No duplicate data maintenance. No complicated handovers between marketing and sales.\r\n\r\nThis means you save:\r\n* Time in setup and maintenance\r\n* Money through fewer tool costs\r\n* Stress in day-to-day business\r\n* Support effort for technical problems\r\n* Sources of error due to unstable integrations\r\n\r\nInstead of a tool stack, a clear, continuous process is created \u2013 from the first click to the next action.\r\n\r\n\ud83d\udc49 Sounds too good to be true?",
